{
  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_031 (multimodal, scvi_n200, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.678 acc, only modestly above RNA-only scvi_n200 (config_005, 0.650). ResNet50 alone is very weak (0.208), raising the question of whether the image modality has meaningful additional signal that ResNet50 simply cannot extract. Question: config_037 swaps the image encoder from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L while holding all other settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion) identical to config_031. This isolates the image-encoder effect. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It is a clean single-variable extension of the current best configuration, directly testing whether the modest +0.028 gain from adding ResNet50 reflects a ceiling in the image encoder or a true ceiling in the image modality's complementary signal. (2) If ViT-L substantially improves over ResNet50, it identifies a promising direction for further multimodal optimization; if it does not, it tells us the image modality contributes little beyond RNA and we should focus remaining budget on RNA-side improvements. (3) Under a limited budget, resolving whether the image channel is worth further investment is more consequential than confirming the already-suggested avgpool>transformer aggregation preference."
}

